{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>How much more those who dwell in houses of clay</b> — a fortiori: those who dwell in houses of clay. But what seems right to me: that \"His servants and His angels\" are the supernal beings, which have no body, while the bodies and souls of human beings are hewn from them, and \"those who dwell in houses of clay\" are the bodies, whose foundation is in dust." "<b>Are crushed</b> — the matter of houses of clay: they crush those who dwell in them, because the body perishes like a moth. And most of the commentators interpreted:" "<b>Before a moth</b> — before the sun. And he said: כי עש, like ועיש על בניה תנחם, and they are seven stars near the northern axle, like שש and שיש. And the meaning: all the days that ʿAyish exists."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra draws on the ancient identification of עש (ʿAyish) as a constellation; the cited phrase ועיש על בניה תנחם is not a biblical verse but appears to be a paraphrase or quotation from astronomical tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:48.879048018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}